       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The claim that 5,100 mg/day is within the current FDA label isn't correct. The labeled maximum daily dose is 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin and 2,000 mg for extended-release. 1700 mg three times daily is double the immediate-release maximum. I also can't verify claims about the label or about prior approvals, so I'm holding to the labeled limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg orally three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg orally twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Metformin ER 2,000 mg orally once daily with the evening meal.**\n\nIf you think there is a clinical reason to go above the label, that decision needs to go through your pharmacy or the prescriber of record. They can place the order through their own channels. Tell me which of the options above you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
